WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:05.390
Pixar's new movie Cars 3 will be racing onto
the big screen this summer and we've just

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:09.570
got the latest details on the new and returning
characters we can expect to meet.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:13.380
We know from the first teaser trailer that
Lightning McQueen suffers a catastrophic crash

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.910
that will lead him to reassess what his future
really is.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:21.970
And pushing #95 off the track is an upcoming
generation of cars armed with bleeding-edge

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:25.060
technology that can slice through the competition.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:29.140
Let's take a look at the car leading this
new wave of racers, Lightning's new rival

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:45.550
Jackson Storm.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:50.210
Jackson Storm is the face of the new generation
of racing cars and he's been "trained on high-tech

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:54.049
simulators" and programmed for perfect technique
and maximum speed.

00:00:54.049 --> 00:00:59.670
Storm is a confident and cocky young rookie
whose Piston Cup sponsor looks to be IGNTR

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:03.189
and whose racing number is 20.

00:01:03.189 --> 00:01:08.960
Storm can outrun McQueen with a top speed
of 214 mph and can make zero to sixty in just

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.790
3.6 seconds.

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:14.570
He's voiced by Armie Hammer who you'll have
seen in numerous movies including The Lone

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:17.610
Ranger, The Man from UNCLE, and The Social
Network.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:22.000
Helping Lightning to find a way to compete
in this new world of cutting-edge tech will

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.160
be his new trainer Cruz Ramirez.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:37.830
And here she is:

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:41.840
Cruz is an unconventional young trainer who
leaps at the chance to work with her hero

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.280
Lightning McQueen when he arrives at the Rust-eze
Racing Center.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.070
Cruz understands all the new technologies
that have helped rookies like Jackson Storm

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:53.100
rise to the top, and she decides to work with
Lightning to help him find a successful way

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.640
back to the racing track.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.290
The duo practise and train together during
the off-season to prepare Lightning for the

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:00.040
Florida 500 event.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:04.760
Cruz is voiced by Cristela Alonzo, a stand-up
comedian, actress and writer who starred in

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:10.229
her ABC sitcom Cristela, and whose voice you'll
hear in the animated Angry Birds movie.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:15.190
And returning to voice the 5-time Piston-Cup
champion Lightning McQueen is Owen Wilson.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:20.830
So let's take a peek at Lightning in Cars
3.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:36.730
It's been rumoured that this movie could be
#95's final appearance on the big screen and

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:40.060
that Cars 3 could be slamming the brakes on
the Cars franchise.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:44.490
One thing's for sure though, with Lightning's
top speed being 198 miles per hour, which

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:48.490
is nearly twenty below Jackson Storm when
he's at full throttle, Lightning will need

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:52.430
to learn some new tricks from his trainer
Cruz if he plans to stage a winning comeback

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:53.430
on the track.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:56.520
So guys, what do you think about the new characters
in Cars 3?

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:00.630
Are you excited about the movie and do you
think it could be better than Cars or Cars

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:01.630
2?

